# Claude Code local machine settings (permission allowlist, not shared)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Local dev-server launch config for the in-editor preview. Tool-specific
# and machine-local on purpose: the repo's portability rule (CLAUDE.md)
# keeps every durable decision in plain markdown, so nothing that matters
# may live in a file only one assistant reads.
.claude/launch.json

# Emergent build-tool metadata (pre-conversion tooling, deleted in roadmap 0.1)
.emergent/

# Screenshot output from scripts/shoot-dashboard.mjs — regenerated on demand,
# never committed. The OUT env var lets a session write elsewhere (roadmap 2.4
# used shots-2.4/ to keep a before/after pair side by side), so the glob covers
# those too.
shots/
shots-*/

# Rendered email output from scripts/render-emails.mjs — regenerated on demand
# (--accent= to check another tenant, --out= to keep two side by side), never
# committed. The SCRIPT is the artefact; the HTML is what you look at once.
email-preview/
email-preview-*/
email-new/
email-new-*/

# Reference screenshots — evidence for the design phase, kept local on purpose.
# 21 MB of other people's websites; the repo is public and history is forever.
# Owner decision 2026-08-29. Cited by filename in docs/references/ANALYSIS.md.
screenshots/

# Local tooling config for the impeccable design hook. NOT tracked, on purpose:
# CLAUDE.md requires that no tool-specific mechanism carry a decision, because
# the owner expects to move to a different coding agent. Both suppressions in it
# are DUPLICATES — the reasoning that matters lives beside the code:
#   .sheet's height transition   -> a comment at that rule in app/src/theme.css
#   Arial in the email templates -> the header of
#                                   supabase/functions/_shared/emailTemplates.ts
.impeccable/

# Ids the seed writes down for the sweeps (roadmap 2.14 step 3). The customer's
# plan page is reached by a membership UUID and `sweep-booking-steps.mjs` has
# no session and no service key with which to find one — so `seed-demo.mjs`
# leaves them here. Regenerated on every seed and specific to whichever
# database was seeded, which is exactly why it is not committed.
scripts/demo-refs.json
